statement:
Let $X$ be Noetherian and $E/\mathbf Q_\ell$ finite, with valuation ring $\cO_E$ and uniformizer $\pi_E$ [def-weil-l-adic-coefficient-extension]. Use the coefficient sheaves of [sk-def-sfb-pulled-back-coefficients] on the small pro-étale site [def-weil-pbc-proetale-site], and the derived categories of module sheaves [def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category, def-weil-abstract-derived-category]. Let $K\in D(X_{\mathrm{proét}},\cO_E)$ be derived $\pi_E$-complete [sk-def-pe-derived-completion]. Write
$$K_n=K\otimes^{\mathbf L}_{\cO_{E,X}}(\cO_E/\pi_E^n)_X,$$
using derived extension of scalars [lem-pur-derived-change-of-rings]. For finite coefficients, $\Dbc$ means bounded complexes with constructible cohomology [sk-def-sfb-constructible, def-weil-proetale-constructible-sheaf]. The following are equivalent:

1. $K_1\in\Dbc(X,\cO_E/\pi_E)$;
2. $K_n\in\Dbc(X,\cO_E/\pi_E^n)$ for every $n\ge1$, and the cohomology of the $K_n$ lies in one interval $[r,s]$ independent of $n$.

Thus the first-reduction condition in the integral criterion (blueprint unit sk-prop-integral-criterion) is equivalent to the all-reductions and uniform-amplitude condition in [def-weil-derived-complete-integral-detailed] for the bounded constructible derived-complete integral category.
